# CMPXCHG—Compare and Exchange -- override
# The manual's Flags Affected says CF, PF, AF, SF, OF (and ZF) are "set
# according to the results of the comparison operation", but its Operation
# has no subtraction to take them from; this adds the comparison the
# Description names ("compares the value in the AL, AX, EAX, or RAX register
# with the first operand").
#
# ZF: the manual sets it in its Operation ('ZF := 1' / 'ZF := 0'); the
# comparison's subtraction (above) gives the same ZF, so it is committed
# with the other flags here (it wasn't: found by tests/diff).
# The failing case's write-back 'DEST := TEMP' is a memory operand's locked
# write cycle; a register destination is left alone, as processors do -- a
# 32-bit write would zero-extend it in 64-bit mode (SDM errata E-18).
@operation
TEMP := DEST;
CMPTEMP := accumulator - TEMP;
ModifyStatusFlags;
IF accumulator = TEMP
    THEN
        DEST := SRC;
    ELSE
        accumulator := TEMP;
        IF MemoryOperand THEN DEST := TEMP; FI;
FI;
@flags
The ZF, CF, PF, AF, SF, and OF flags are set according to the result of the comparison.
